Test Case: diskOSImportManagedDiskWithSize
================================================================================

Step: Step 2 - Verify AzureRM Configuration (Baseline Test)

Failed Command: terraform apply -auto-approve -input=false

Error Message:
│ Error: Invalid index
│
│   on azurerm.tf line 11, in resource "azurerm_linux_virtual_machine" "test":
│   11:   os_managed_disk_id = data.azurerm_managed_disks.test.disk.0.id
│     ├────────────────
│     │ data.azurerm_managed_disks.test.disk is empty list of object
│
│ The given key does not identify an element in this collection value: the collection has no elements.

Root Cause Analysis:
This test case is part of a multi-step acceptance test sequence:
1. TestAccLinuxVirtualMachine_diskOSImportManagedDiskUpdateSize first creates a VM with delete_os_disk_on_deletion = false
2. Then removes the VM but keeps the OS disk 
3. Finally imports that existing managed disk into a new VM (this test case)

The test configuration expects an existing managed disk to already be present in the resource group (referenced via data.azurerm_managed_disks.test.disk.0.id), but when run as a standalone test, no disk exists.

This test case cannot be run independently - it requires the managed disk to be created by a previous test step (diskOSBasicNoDelete) and left behind after VM deletion (osDiskImportTemplateWithProvider).

Conclusion:
This is NOT a module implementation error. The test case is designed as part of a sequential multi-step test and cannot be validated as a standalone configuration. The test extraction process has isolated a configuration that is inherently dependent on prior state from other test steps.

Recommendation:
Mark this test case as "invalid" for standalone testing. These import scenarios would need to be tested as complete sequences if import functionality is to be validated.
